.TH WORDCOUNT 3 "September 2026" "Version 0.3.1" "MyUtils Library Manual"
.SH NAME
wordCount \- count lines, words, and characters in a file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <myfilefunctions.h>
.sp
.BI "int wordCount(const char *" filename ", int *" lines ", int *" words ", int *" chars ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B wordCount()
function reads the file specified by
.I filename
and computes the total number of lines, words, and characters. The results are stored in the memory locations pointed to by
.I lines
,
.I words
, and
.I chars
.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, or -1 if the file cannot be opened.
